# <type>(<optional scope>): <subject>
#
# https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
#
# type      feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore,
#           revert. feat and fix describe behaviour; the rest do not.
# scope     optional, e.g. templates, vars, policy, resources/pods
# subject   imperative mood, no trailing period, under 72 characters
#
# Body: wrap at 80. Explain why the change was made, not what it does — the
# diff already shows what. Optional; a one-line change does not need one.
#
# Breaking changes: append ! after the type/scope (feat!: ...) and add a
# BREAKING CHANGE: <description> trailer below.
#
# Trailers can route downstream CI, so keep them exact:
#   Refs: <ticket>
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
#
# Lines beginning with # are stripped. gitlint checks this message at
# commit-msg and .gitlint is authoritative for the type list and line limits.
